{
  "description": "Submit a turn proposal to the Indy_Reads governor. The governor validates, sanitizes authority-bearing fields, and decides. Output is a proposal, never an action.",
  "name": "submit_proposal",
  "parameters": {
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "description": "The fields an LLM tool call may set on a proposal.\n\nLanguage-only contract (depenaudit K-1, 2026-10-09): the model produces\nprose, never classifications. `intent`, `claim`, `hypothesis`, and\n`requested_action` were deleted — production code never read them; the\ndeterministic governor owns classification (`classify_intent`,\n`evaluate_utterance` in governor.rs). Authority-bearing fields\n(`authority`, `verified`, `execute`, `claim_status`) remain deliberately\nabsent — the governor strips and records them; they are not part of any\ntool contract.",
    "properties": {
      "reply": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "response_style": {
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "reply"
    ],
    "title": "ProposalTool",
    "type": "object"
  }
}
